        "comments": "The assembly bRipRip1.hap1.1 is based on 39x Oxford Nanopore data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial Oxford Nanopore assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. MicroFinder was used to order scaffolds prior to curation. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Chromosomes Z and W were identified by copy number in the diploid assembly and by HiC signal. The order and orientation of scaffolds in the following regions is uncertain: Chromosome 2 10.52-13.72Mb; Chromosome 5 6.46-8.63Mb; Chromosome 7 2.78-7.02Mb; Chromosome W 9.34-28.96Mb; Chromosome Z 47.69-52.41Mb",
